    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and all its tests pass with a green build.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the optional, region-validated `postcode` field for owners end-to-end.\n\n**Contract / schema**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added an optional `postcode` (pattern `^[0-9]{4}$`) to the shared `OwnerFields` schema, so it flows into both the request DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and the response DTO (`OwnerDto`, via `allOf`) that MapStruct maps by name.\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added the `postcode` column/field with getter/setter.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `postcode` column (tests run on hsqldb).\n\n**Validation (the rule)**\n- New `Postcode` helper (`function/owner/Postcode.java`) \u2014 `normalize(postcode, city)`: absent (null/blank) \u2192 `null` (accepted); present \u2192 must be exactly 4 digits, and when the city maps to a known region (Sydney=NSW 2000-2099, Melbourne=VIC 3000-3099, Brisbane=QLD 4000-4099) it must fall in range; unknown-region cities accept any 4-digit value. Invalid \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n- New checked `InvalidPostcodeException` + `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler` (responds 400) + escalation YAML, mirroring the existing email/telephone pattern.\n\n**Wiring**\n- `ValidateOwnerFields` (POST) and `ValidateOwner` (PUT) now call `Postcode.normalize(...)`, storing the trimmed value back; `BuildOwner` (POST, via mapper) and `ApplyOwner` (PUT) persist it.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest` \u2014 3/3 pass (stores valid postcode, accepts owner without postcode, rejects malformed with 400); `BUILD SUCCESS` for the full `mvn test`.",
